From: cnjn
Subject: [PATCH] fw4: keep multicast streams out of the flowtable

A flowtable entry has one output device and outlives the multicast route
that made it: once a routed multicast stream (IPv6 in practice) was
offloaded, it bypassed the multicast routing table, so receivers leaving,
TTL thresholds and further downstream interfaces had no effect, and
anything at the ingress of the routed device (e.g. a tc fast path) never
saw the stream again. Offload unicast TCP and UDP only.

---
--- a/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
@@ -135,7 +135,8 @@
 		type filter hook forward priority filter; policy {{ fw4.forward_policy(true) }};
 
 {% if (length(flowtable_devices) > 0): %}
-		meta l4proto { tcp, udp } flow offload @ft;
+		meta nfproto ipv4 meta l4proto { tcp, udp } ip daddr != 224.0.0.0/4 flow offload @ft;
+		meta nfproto ipv6 meta l4proto { tcp, udp } ip6 daddr != ff00::/8 flow offload @ft;
 {% endif %}
 {% fw4.includes('chain-prepend', 'forward') %}
 		ct state vmap { established : accept, related : accept{% if (fw4.default_option("drop_invalid")): %}, invalid : drop{% endif %} } comment "!fw4: Handle forwarded flows"
